messages:
anna: heads-up folks — hit a reproducible issue in the kotlin sampleapp when streaming gzipped uploads on emulators. Behavior: sometimes server sees duplicate POSTs; second POST uses a refreshed token. minimal repro attached below.

anna: sequence: streaming RequestBody -> socket write fails (EPIPE) -> our Authenticator runs to refresh token -> OkHttp internal recovery also enqueues a retry -> two POSTs observed ~50-200ms apart.

anna: sample RequestBody: 
```kotlin
val body = object: RequestBody() {
  override fun contentType() = "application/gzip".toMediaType()
  override fun writeTo(sink: BufferedSink) {
    GzipSink(sink).use { gz -> inputStream.source().use { it.readAll(gz) } }
  }
}
```

kai: the root cause is a race between two independent retry paths: (1) OkHttp's connection-recovery when write errors, (2) Authenticator creating a follow-up after 401. Streaming bodies aren't rewindable so replaying is unsafe. Check `retryOnConnectionFailure` and avoid blocking IO threads in Authenticator (runBlocking).

diego: workaround I used: disable retryOnConnectionFailure on the upload client and implement single-flight token refresh (Mutex) in a higher-level interceptor so Authenticator doesn't block okhttp threads. Also considered buffering a small prefix (8KB) so short retries don't resend whole payload.

anna: CI note: reproducible-upload branch triggered UploadRetryRaceTest failure on emulator-14 matrix. ci-bot: see job 5123 logs.

ci-bot: CI failure: UploadRetryRaceTest failed consistently on api-33 emulator.

anna: plan: (1) update sampleapp upload client to set retryOnConnectionFailure=false, (2) add docs in devex about streaming + retry interactions, (3) show Mutex-based single-flight refresh snippet and small prefix-buffer idea. Will open PR and tag @kai @diego for review. :thumbsup:
